# Everything here is LF, in the object store AND in every working tree.
#
# This repo is developed on Windows with core.autocrlf=true, so without this
# rule every file is checked out with CRLF while the blobs themselves stay LF.
# Prettier's `endOfLine` defaults to "lf", so `npx prettier --check .` then
# reports every file in the repo as unformatted — 208 of them here, none of
# which had anything wrong with its formatting. That buries any real finding and
# makes the check worthless, which is exactly what had happened.
#
# The blobs are already LF, so this only pins the working tree to match what is
# committed; it does not rewrite anything.
#
# Git attributes are per-repository and do not follow into or out of a
# submodule, which is why the monorepo root and administrative-document each
# carry their own copy of the equivalent rule rather than inheriting one.
* text=auto eol=lf

# The one genuinely binary asset in the tree. `text=auto` would detect it, but
# saying so costs nothing and removes the guess.
*.ico binary
